There are, IMNSHO, some significant barriers in the exchange of bones [as by 
Hearse] simply due to differences in versions that ought not to matter.

The Linux users ought to be able to exchange bones with the Windoze users.

The users of PCs ought to be able to exchange bones with the users of Macs.

Those wbo have the mail daemon turned off ought to be able to exchange bones 
with those who have it turned on.

None of this is possible, because of the way that bones are stored.

There are, of course, some limits -- if you have the Hell Patch and you fall 
to Lilith, how can you pass bones to someone for whom Lilith does not 
exist?  Beyond that, though, the current restrictions are not reasonable.  
It doesn't have to be like this.


